(1161, NULL, NULL, '019630', 'Ms.', 'นางสาว', 'อชิรญา  เนาวรัตน์กิตติกุล', 'ACHIRAYA  NAOWARATKITTIKUL', 'G000', NULL, 'General Office', 'G200', NULL, 'Human Resources & Adminstration', 'G2PS', NULL, 'Personnel & Salary Admin', '302', '302', '301', 'Asst Supervisor', 'Asst Supervisor', '1. Job Header\n1.1 Position: Supervisor\n1.2 Position Description: G2PS-Payroll\n1.3 Company MIL\n1.4 Level - L700\n1.5 Division - G000\n1.6 Department - G200\n1.7 Section - G2PS\n1.8 Position Backup - Assistant Manager\n1.9 Position report to this role - Officer, Senior Clerk\n1.10 Position Report to - Assistant Manager\n1.11 Higher Line of Order - Manager\n\n2. Role and Responsibilities (Key Responsibility / Task)\n* Payroll Processing: Manage the end-to-end payroll process\n* Compliance: Stay abreast of local regulations governing payroll practices and ensure company compliance with all applicable laws. This includes tax regulations, wage laws, and reporting requirements.\n* Systems Management: Utilize payroll software/systems effectively to streamline processes and enhance accuracy. Implement improvements or upgrades as necessary to optimize efficiency.\n* Recordkeeping: Maintain accurate records of payroll transactions, including employee deductions, bonuses, benefits, and other compensation-related information.\n* Reporting: Generate regular reports related to payroll data.\n* Employee Support: Serve as a primary point of contact for employees regarding payroll inquiries or concerns. Provide timely and accurate responses and escalate issues as necessary.\n* Training and Development: Train and mentor payroll staff as needed, ensuring high competence and professionalism within the team.\n* Continuous Improvement: Identify opportunities for process improvements and implement best practices to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of the payroll function.\n* Collaboration: Work closely with HR, Finance, and other relevant departments to ensure seamless coordination and alignment of payroll processes with overall business objectives.\n* Ad Hoc Projects: Participate in special projects or initiatives related to payroll or broader organizational goals as assigned.\n\n3. Job Competencies\n3.1 Knowledge\n* A bachelor\'s degree in HR, business administration, or a related field is preferred.\n3.2 Skills\n* Minimum of 3 years of experience in payroll processing and administration, with at least 3 years in a supervisory or managerial role.\n3.3 Personality Traits\n* Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with keen attention to detail.\n* Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to interact effectively with employees at all levels of the organization.\n* Demonstrated ability to prioritize tasks, meet deadlines, and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment.', 'To replace Ms. Sirachcha - the Payroll Supervisor, who will retire at the end of Dec 2024.', 'L700', 'Below Section Head (TH)', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2019-03-11 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Passed', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2024-03-01 07:57:00', NULL),
